   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "שְׁלֹשָׁה שֶׁלָּווּ מֵאֶחָד יַחְזִיר לַמַּלְוֶה וְכוּ׳. דְּאִי סָלְקָא דַעְתָּךְ דְּלֹוִין נִינְהוּ, מַאי בָּעוּ גַּבֵּי הֲדָדֵי?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the promissory notes make reference to the loans of «three» people «who borrowed from one» person, the one who found them «must return» them «to the creditor.» The Gemara explains: The reason for this is «that if it enters your mind that these» promissory notes «belong to» the «debtors, what are they doing together?»"
  }
